# PartStateReport: generated by tools/generate_interfaces.py from more_generic_models 0.1.0. Do not edit.
# The state of one part of the vehicle that judges or delivers something: ``part`` its label, ``kind`` ``monitor`` or ``payload``,
# ``health`` in ``interfaces.HEALTHS``. For a monitor that judged a breach: ``text_kind`` the word of the breach (``max_depth``,
# ``min_altitude``, ``region``, ``timeout``, ... the monitor's ``TEXT_KIND``; empty when none) and ``value`` the number it judged
# (NaN: none; m for a depth or an altitude, s for a time). Health of a monitor: ``ok`` while it holds no verdict, ``degraded``
# while it holds a WARN verdict, ``fault`` while it holds a PAUSE or an ABORT verdict.
#
# Frames (owner decision): positions NED about the scenario origin (x north, y east), body quantities FRD, angles in rad from
# north clockwise, time in s on the scenario clock.
std_msgs/Header header  # stamp = t rounded to ns; frame_id map_ned for positions
uint64 stream_seq  # publication counter per vehicle across all report types (restores the drain order)
float64 t  # unit: s; the sample instant on the scenario clock, exactly
string part
string kind
string health
string text_kind
float64[<=1] value  # optional: empty = none (the monitor judged no number); send one value to set it. MGM default nan; GAP: unit and frame not given by the library
